  "lineage": "Kingston recordings of the late 1950s cut for sound-system operators such as Clement 'Coxsone' Dodd and Duke Reid, first as exclusive sound-system records and then as local singles, modelled on US rhythm and blues. Jamaican players stressed the afterbeat of the shuffle rhythm, the step that led directly to ska around 1960.",
